       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">EDUCATION</span> · Education (aggregate) · 2026-10-30 · editor 8/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Bengaluru to Host DIDAC India, Asia's Large Education Gathering</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Education</span> <span>#Skilling</span> <span>#Bengaluru</span> <span>#DIDAC India</span></div>
       <p>Bengaluru is poised to host DIDAC India, an event recognized as one of Asia's largest education and skilling gatherings. This significant event will convene key players in the education sector, as reported by India Education Diary.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-30/bengaluru-to-host-didac-india-asias-large-education-gatherin.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>DIDAC India aims to attract a substantial audience, targeting over 30,000 visitors from more than 40 countries. The gathering in Bengaluru is specifically focused on education and skilling, according to the India Education Diary summary.</p><p>What to watch: Specific dates and agenda for the upcoming DIDAC India event.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft accurately captures the core details from the source summary. It is concise and reports the key figures provided.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://news.google.?oc=5&amp;hl=en-US&amp;gl=US&amp;ceid=US:en" rel="noopener">Education (aggregate)</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
