       <h1>Centre to Tap IITs, NITs for Nuclear Tech Courses</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Nuclear Energy</span> <span>#IITs</span> <span>#NITs</span> <span>#Education</span></div>
       <p>The Centre has announced plans to tap into the expertise of IITs and NITs to develop nuclear technology courses. This initiative is aimed at supporting India's goal of achieving 100 GW of nuclear power capacity.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-30/centre-to-tap-iits-nits-for-nuclear-tech-courses.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The move signals a strategic collaboration between premier engineering institutions and the government's energy sector. By leveraging the academic infrastructure of these institutes, the government intends to accelerate the development of specialized talent required for the nuclear sector.</p><p>No specific dates, eligibility criteria, or official links were provided in the source summary. The announcement focuses on the institutional partnership rather than immediate admission details.</p><p>What to watch: Official notifications from IITs and NITs regarding specific course structures and admission timelines.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft captures the core of the brief announcement accurately, though it is thin due to the limited source material.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://news.google.?oc=5" rel="noopener">Education (aggregate)</a></li></ul>
