     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-30 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Election Campaign Concludes in Tirupati District</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Campaigning for urban local body elections in Tirupati district ended on Friday evening as candidates concluded final canvassing efforts. Officials have completed the randomization of police personnel for polling duty, and a dedicated control room has been established at the Tirupati Collectorate to monitor the process and handle public complaints.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-30/election-campaign-concludes-in-tirupati-district.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>To facilitate voting for election staff, special centers have been set up at MPDO offices across the district. Polling officers and assistant polling officers are scheduled to cast their postal ballots on November 2 between 10 am and 5 pm.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief covers all key logistics mentioned in the source regarding the campaign conclusion and polling procedures.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/andhra-pradesh/election-campaign-draws-to-a-close-in-tirupati-district/article71646148.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
