       <h1>Expert Committee to Review Doctor Leave at Government Medical Colleges</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Health Policy</span> <span>#Medical Education</span> <span>#Government</span></div>
       <p>The Union health ministry has established an expert committee to examine the existing vacation and academic/on-duty leave arrangements for Central Health Service (CHS) teaching doctors. This development, confirmed by official documents, indicates a review of current policies impacting medical faculty.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-30/expert-committee-to-review-doctor-leave-at-government-medica.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The committee held its inaugural meeting on August 31. Its mandate is to scrutinize the various leave provisions, including those for vacations and professional development, afforded to teaching doctors within government medical colleges.</p><p>What to watch: The committee's recommendations could lead to significant changes in leave policies for CHS teaching doctors.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft accurately reports the committee's formation and purpose based on the provided summary.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
