       <h1>Gail's net profit zooms two-fold to ₹4,724 crore on robust volumes</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#GAIL</span> <span>#Net Profit</span> <span>#Q2</span> <span>#IPO</span></div>
       <p>GAIL (India) Limited has reported a significant surge in its Q2 net profit, which jumped by 138% to reach ₹4,724 crore. This substantial increase in earnings highlights a robust performance for the quarter.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-30/gails-net-profit-zooms-two-fold-to-4724-crore-on-robust-volu.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The impressive financial results were primarily supported by strong volumes in both gas transmission and marketing segments. Additionally, the company's board of directors has approved plans to list its subsidiary, GAIL Gas, through an Initial Public Offering (IPO), indicating strategic expansion.</p><p>What to watch: The progress of the GAIL Gas IPO and future volume performance.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article concisely presents the key financial figures and the board's decision regarding the IPO as per the source.</p>
