     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-30 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Karnataka Government Advances Winter Session to November 30</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The Karnataka government has moved the start of the State Legislative Assembly's Winter Session at Suvarna Soudha in Belagavi to November 30, with proceedings scheduled to conclude on December 11. The session was advanced from its original December 7 start date, reportedly due to the anticipated announcement of upcoming Gram Panchayat elections.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-30/karnataka-government-advances-winter-session-to-november-30.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Local officials, including the Deputy Commissioner and Police Commissioner, have begun comprehensive preparations for the event. Various committees have been established to manage essential services, including security, transportation, guest hospitality, facility maintenance, and road repairs, ensuring the venue is fully prepared for the assembly's arrival.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately relays the scheduling change and the administrative preparations mentioned in the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/karnataka/suvarna-soudha-in-belagavi-to-host-winter-session-starting-nov-30/article71645133.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
