       <h1>Rajeev Siddhartha and Kirti Kulhari’s Kinaare Set for DIFF Premiere</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#entertainment</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Actor Rajeev Siddhartha is set to debut at the Dharamshala International Film Festival (DIFF) on October 30 with the film Kinaare. The project marks Kirti Kulhari’s debut as a producer, with both actors starring in the lead roles. Written and directed by Akbar and Azam Qadri, the film was recently completed in January.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-30/rajeev-siddhartha-and-kirti-kulharis-kinaare-set-for-diff-pr.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Siddhartha describes the film as meditative and slow-paced, drawing comparisons to Iranian cinema for its focus on silence and stillness rather than frantic editing. The actor expressed gratitude for the festival premiere, noting that the story’s deliberate pacing and emotional depth allow for nuanced performances where silence often communicates more than dialogue.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief is accurate and well-structured, though it omits that the film was shot in 18 days, which adds depth to the production context.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/news/features/exclusive-rajeev-siddhartha-ecstatic-about-his-film-festival-debut-at-dharamshalas-diff-compares-kirti-kulharis-maiden-production-kinaare-to-iranian-cinema-it-doesnt-ha/" rel="noopener">Bollywood Hungama</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
