     <article class="story single" data-beat="cricket">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">CRICKET</span> · Crictracker · 2026-10-30 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Rohit Sharma Explains Origins of Iconic Jersey Number 45</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#cricket</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>India cricket captain Rohit Sharma revealed that his choice of jersey number 45 was influenced by his mother after he was unable to secure his preferred digits. During his early career, Rohit wore number 19, which he utilized during his Under-19 tenure. However, upon reaching the senior national team, he discovered that number 19 was already occupied by then-captain Rahul Dravid.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-30/rohit-sharma-explains-origins-of-iconic-jersey-number-45.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Faced with the unavailability of his previous number, Rohit sought guidance from his mother to select a new identifier. This necessity led to the adoption of number 45, which has since become an iconic part of his identity in international cricket.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurately captures the narrative of the number 45's origin, though it slightly simplifies the mother's role (she suggested the sum of 9, and he finalized 45 based on aesthetics).</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.crictracker.com/cricket-news/rohit-sharma-reveals-how-his-mother-helped-him-to-choose-45-as-his-jersey-number/" rel="noopener">Crictracker</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
