     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-30 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Seeman Open to Support from DMK and AIADMK for Ambasamudram Byelection</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Naam Tamilar Katchi leader Seeman has indicated a willingness to accept electoral support from the DMK and AIADMK if they back his candidacy in the upcoming Ambasamudram Assembly byelection. Seeman remarked that a candidate seeking victory would not reject such offers, clarifying that his past criticisms of these parties were ideological rather than personal.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-30/seeman-open-to-support-from-dmk-and-aiadmk-for-ambasamudram-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>While no formal alliance has been announced, DMK president M.K. Stalin declined to directly address the possibility of backing Seeman, stating the byelection date must be scheduled first. Seeman, who has polled 8.5% of the vote share, emphasized his intent to contest the seat regardless of other parties' positions.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately reports Seeman's stance and the context of the potential byelection.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
