     <article class="story single" data-beat="world">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">WORLD</span> · The Hindu World · 2026-10-30 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge conf" title="Reported by The Hindu World, News18 World">confirmed by 2 sources</span></div>
       <h1>Sir Patrick Stewart, Star Trek and X-Men Star, Dies at 86</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Entertainment</span> <span>#Obituary</span> <span>#Film</span> <span>#Television</span></div>
       <p>Sir Patrick Stewart, the celebrated British actor known globally for his roles as Captain Jean-Luc Picard in &quot;Star Trek: The Next Generation&quot; and Professor Charles Xavier in the &quot;X-Men&quot; films, has died at the age of 86. The Hindu World reported his passing at his Los Angeles home, while News18 World noted it followed a battle with Alzheimer's and Lewy Body Dementia. A statement on his X account confirmed he passed &quot;in the loving care of his beloved wife Sunny following a brief and poignant journey&quot; with these conditions.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-30/sir-patrick-stewart-star-trek-and-x-men-star-dies-at-86.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Born on July 13, 1940, in Mirfield, Yorkshire, Stewart rose from poverty in England, becoming an actor at 18. He gained early acclaim in the 1960s as a member of the Royal Shakespeare Company. Despite initially balking at the role, and friend Ian McKellen advising him against it, Stewart accepted the part of Captain Picard at age 47 for &quot;Star Trek: The Next Generation,&quot; which ran from 1987 to 1994. This role catapulted him to mainstream fame, a journey he continued into his 80s, including in the streaming series &quot;Star Trek: Picard&quot; which began in 2020 when he was 79.</p><p>Stewart also initially hesitated to portray Professor X in the &quot;X-Men&quot; movies, a role he took starting with the first entry in 2000. He told The Guardian in 2022 that the distinction between himself and Picard &quot;became thinner and thinner.&quot; Knighted by Queen Elizabeth II in 2010 for his contributions to drama, Stewart considered being &quot;in that company&quot; with heroes like Laurence Olivier and John Gielgud &quot;the grandest thing that has professionally happened to me.&quot;</p><p>What to watch: The entertainment world awaits further tributes to the late actor's extensive career.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article effectively synthesizes the provided source text and supplementary outlets into a cohesive biography and report on the actor's passing.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>How this was reported · 2 sources</b>
