     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-30 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Telangana Congress credits Revanth Reddy for protecting 550 acres in Miyapur</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>TPCC general secretary Chanagani Dayakar praised Chief Minister A. Revanth Reddy for securing 550 acres of government land in Miyapur. The Supreme Court verdict in the case is being hailed as a victory for the government's legal efforts against encroachment.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-30/telangana-congress-credits-revanth-reddy-for-protecting-550-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Dayakar alleged that the previous BRS administration attempted to transfer valuable government land to private entities. He further demanded that BRS leader K.T. Rama Rao clarify financial transactions involving Trinity Infra Limited and the acquisition of 6,666 vehicles, questioning the transparency of those past dealings.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately summarizes the political accusations and the specific land issue mentioned in the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/telangana/congress-thanks-revanth-for-saving-550-acres/article71644657.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
